[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65542,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Follicular lymphoma (FL) is a malignant lymphoid neoplasm of follicle-centre B&nbsp;cells, typically showing follicular architecture.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65543,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>9690/3 Follicular lymphoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65544,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2A80.Z &amp; XH3FE9 Follicular lymphoma, unspecified &amp; Mature B-cell lymphomas</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65545,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65546,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65547,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The most frequently involved female genital tract (FGT) sites include the ovaries/adnexa, vulva, and vagina {28284518; 11444509; 21997689; 16224219}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65548,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most cases present with symptoms and signs related to a localized mass and appear to be primary, but secondary involvement by systemic FL is also seen.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65549,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FL accounts for 10&ndash;20% of all lymphomas of the FGT. The disease affects adults. Other epidemiological features or risk factors have not been well established.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65550,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65551,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "<p>Pathogenesis has been best studied in ovarian/adnexal FLs in which one of two distinct biological subsets, characterized by primary presentation and secondary involvement, has been identified {21997689}. Primary cases are of higher grade, often show a diffuse component, and lack IGH/<em>BCL2</em> rearrangement, whereas secondary cases show typical features of systemic FL with IGH/<em>BCL2</em> rearrangement.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-08-04T15:44:40"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65552,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65553,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The morphology of FL in the FGT is comparable to that in nodal and other extranodal sites. Primary ovarian cases, compared with secondary involvement by systemic disease, tend to have a more mixed diffuse and follicular growth pattern and higher-grade cytology. FL cells express pan&ndash;B-cell markers (CD20, CD79a), BCL6, and (variably) CD10. BCL2 expression is variable and correlates with IGH/<em>BCL2</em> translocation {21997689}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65554,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65555,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The characteristic t(14;18)(q32;q21) translocation is typically seen in secondary involvement by FL, whereas primary cases often lack this translocation.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65556,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> a lymphoid proliferation with cytological features of follicle-centre cells; at least focal atypical follicle formation (crowding, lack of polarization, lack of tingible-body macrophages); a B-lineage neoplasm with expression of follicle-centre cell markers.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65557,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Lymphoid neoplasms are staged according to the Lugano classification {25113753}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65558,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 484,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>FL of the FGT is an indolent disease associated with a 5-year cancer-specific survival rate of 88.6% {28284518}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-10T10:08:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]